+# Add ROCm support if available.
+#
+# Every VRAM path in this plugin sits behind HAVE_CUDA, which is defined only
+# when a CUDA toolkit is found -- so on a ROCm machine the backend compiles
+# host-memory-only and getSupportedMems() can never return VRAM_SEG, whatever
+# the rail manager detected. That is a build-time gate, not a device or
+# libfabric limitation: libfabric's verbs provider advertises FI_HMEM for a
+# RoCE device, and FI_HMEM_ROCR with fi_mr_attr.device.rocr has been available
+# since libfabric v2.3.
+#
+# No ROCm dependency is linked. The ROCr path needs no HIP calls from this
+# plugin: the CUDA context workaround stays CUDA-only (ROCr has no equivalent),
+# and the device handle is set in the rail layer. This flag therefore only
+# un-gates code, which is why it can key off the path rather than a found
+# dependency.
+rocm_path_opt = get_option('rocm_path')
+if rocm_path_opt != '' and fs.exists(rocm_path_opt)
+    compile_flags += ['-DHAVE_ROCM']
+    message('LIBFABRIC plugin: ROCm VRAM support enabled from ' + rocm_path_opt)
+endif
